        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கலந்துரையாடு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கலந்துரையாடு — kalanturaiyāṭu — \"to talk over; to discuss together\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மாணவர்கள் இந்தத் தலைப்பைப் பற்றிக் கலந்துரையாடினார்கள். māṇavarkaḷ intat talaippaip paṟṟik kalanturaiyāṭiṉārkaḷ. The students talked over this topic."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): கலந்துரையாடினேன், kalanturaiyāṭiṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The topic takes -ஐப் பற்றி; the others -உடன்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கலந்துரையாடு (kalanturaiyāṭu) is native: kalantu, \"having mixed, joined\", from kala (DEDR 1299), urai, \"word\" (DEDR 648), and āṭu, \"to move, play\" (DEDR 347): to exchange words together."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
